From 1973d6f3c1ba4242ac9f085c8e22caf4467e32e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Respawn guard: a PR owner requeued by a core update
 after publishing gets one continuation

Production 2026-11-13 (t_01a1d1d7998cda2a): run 20713 opened and reported its
own PR #1783, then the hermes-sync core updater requeued it 9 min later
("restart-safe worker requeue", a pause per kanban_core_update_requeue). The
PR comment post-dated every handoff, latest_ended_run_skipping_requeues found
the earlier `continued` run 20711 (ended before the comment), and no
dependency park existed, so active_pr held the card in ready with no worker
until an operator `kanban resume`.

New hermes_cli/kanban_requeued_publisher.continues(), consulted by
active_pr_reason after _handed_off_after, grants exactly one continuation when
ALL hold:
- the newest holding PR comment, and every holding PR comment written since
  that run was claimed, was written by that run: one `commented` event per row,
  identified by writer_run_uid on a synced schema (never the remappable
  integer) or writer_run_id on an unsynced one, mapped through the same
  _comment_events row matching _foreign_pr_comment_ids uses;
- that run ended as a core-update requeue (is_core_update_requeue: no crash,
  timeout or other reclaim);
- its profile is the card's current assignee;
- every run claimed after it is skipped (another core-update requeue or an
  attested unused grant, as everywhere else in kanban_core_update_requeue):
  the next real claim consumes the grant, so its crash or timeout holds again.
Unknown/missing/ambiguous provenance, a second writer (known or unknown), a
chat or other-card author, another profile or a later real run keeps the hold.
Comments from before that run's claim are not re-judged: the guard already
let that claim through. The kanban_core_update_requeue docstring residual is
updated to match. The crash/timeout-of-publisher hold from f1b81aee0d,
db8b5c1168, 80d4591ed6 and 74b9347149 is unchanged.

Proof:
- RED on base: 7 of the new positive tests fail (publisher continuation,
  dispatcher respawn, synced uid path); every hold case passes before and after.
- GREEN: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_core_update_requeue_handoff.py 43 passed.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py): 15/15 killed (every added condition,
  the active_pr_reason hook and the published list).
- Replay over worker-2's real boards (kanban.db + 5 named boards, read-only
  copy, pr_state stubbed OPEN): 178 cards with comments, 5 held before,
  exactly 1 changes: t_01a1d1d7998cda2a (the incident) active_pr -> None.
- Consumers: 74 test files importing the guard/requeue/hold-release/resume
  modules pass.
